  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">R</mi></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;be continuous functions which are twice differentiable on the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Let the values of <math><mi>f</mi></math> and <math><mi>g</mi></math> at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> be as given in the following table:<br />&nbsp;<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math></td>\t\t\t<td>3</td>\t\t\t<td>6</td>\t\t\t<td>0</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>0</td>\t\t\t<td>1</td>\t\t\t<td>-1</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><br />In each of the intervals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#34;</mo></math> never vanishes. Then the correct statement(s) is(are)",
    "image": null
